"# Notes guide\n"
"\n"
"Write notes as Python scripts in the **NumWorks Workshop**, name them `note_xxx.py`, sync, and they appear here. Markdown and LaTeX maths both render.\n"
"\n"
"## Text\n"
"\n"
"Normal, **bold**, *italic* and `code`. Lists:\n"
"\n"
"- a bullet\n"
"- another one\n"
"  - nested\n"
"1. first\n"
"2. second\n"
"\n"
"> A quote block, for definitions or reminders.\n"
"\n"
"---\n"
"\n"
"## Maths\n"
"\n"
"Inline maths with dollars: the roots are $x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}$ and $e^{i\\pi}+1=0$.\n"
"\n"
"Display maths with double dollars:\n"
"\n"
"$$\\sum_{k=1}^{n} k^2 = \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}$$\n"
"\n"
"$$\\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx = \\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^1 = \\frac{1}{3}$$\n"
"\n"
"$$\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin x}{x} = 1, \\quad \\sqrt[3]{27} = 3, \\quad |\\vec{v}| = \\sqrt{v_x^2 + v_y^2}$$\n"
"\n"
"Greek: $\\alpha, \\beta, \\gamma, \\delta, \\theta, \\lambda, \\mu, \\pi, \\sigma, \\omega, \\Delta, \\Sigma, \\Omega$. Relations: $a \\leq b$, $a \\geq b$, $a \\neq b$, $a \\approx b$, $x \\to \\infty$.\n"
"\n"
"## Tables\n"
"\n"
"| Test | Converges when |\n"
"|:-----|:--------------:|\n"
"| Geometric | $|r| < 1$ |\n"
"| p-series | $p > 1$ |\n"
"| Ratio | $\\rho < 1$ |\n"
"\n"
"Start each row with `|`. The row above `|---|` is the header; colons set the alignment.\n"
"\n"
"## Keys\n"
"\n"
"- **Up/Down**: scroll one line. **Left/Right**: previous/next page.\n"
"- **OK**: contents, jump to any heading.\n"
"- Type any letter or digit (Alpha + key) to **search**. EXE or Down: next match, Up: previous, Back: close.\n"
"- **Toolbox**: switch the text size. **Back**: return to the list (the position is remembered).\n"
"\n"
